  "title": "claude: no \"Generated with Claude Code\" footer on PRs (#87)",
  "body": "Closes #87.\n\n## Summary\n\n`home/.claude/settings.shared.json` sets `\"attribution\": {\"pr\": \"\", \"sessionUrl\": false}`. When that key is set, Claude Code returns its value as the whole PR footer, ahead of the default \"Generated with\" line and any surface suffix (seen in the 2.1.311 CLI: `if(y.attribution?.pr!==void 0)return y.attribution.pr`; the setting's schema reads \"Empty string hides attribution\"). Since it's in the shared file, every profile gets it, `remote` (cloud sessions) included. `sessionUrl: false` drops the claude.ai session link the CLI adds to commits and PRs from cloud and Remote Control sessions (schema: \"Set to false to omit the Claude-Session trailer\"). The Co-Authored-By trailer stays.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Sandbox install, `HOME=$(mktemp -d) bin/dotagents install --no-pull --profile <p>`, for remote, mac and vps: the generated `~/.claude/settings.json` holds `\"attribution\":{\"pr\":\"\",\"sessionUrl\":false}`.\n- `mise run check` at `a249731`: exit 0, all 10 checks passed.\n- Not met by this PR: **cloud PR comments**. They end with `_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_`, as on the PR that prompted #87. That string is not in the CLI, and anthropics/claude-code#62791 reports the cloud GitHub integration appending it after the model posts, whatever `attribution` says. No setting reaches it, so #87's comment acceptance waits on the owner's scope decision.\n- Cloud sessions pick up dotagents main on their next container build, so a cloud PR body can only be checked after this lands.\n\n- verifier: same family (Codex out of usage until 2026-11-02). Claude Sonnet 5.5, pass 2 on `a249731`: satisfied.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\nLow. One settings key; removing it brings the footer back.\n\nImpl: cc/opus-5.5/high\n",
